DECISION: **DG7 round 5 outcome on 07af9fba, and the A3.9 residual 1 decision.** Domain PASS and code-security PASS; both verified 922, 941, 970 closed. The qa-verifier run reached a FAIL verdict (its `qa-verifier.md`, findings and verifications are committed) but was killed by a container restart before it wrote `qa-verifier.json`, so its verifications are not imported. New **F-DG7-971** (Medium): the A18 drill and harness fail at D9 when the `*/15` `approval.escalation_scan` starter (or a daily starter) runs on the target between D7 and D9, since mode 2 classifies schedule-triggered executions as unexplained; about 5-7 % of runs fail on the clock alone. The product is correct. **Decision on ADR-0064 A3.9 residual 1 (the ADR leaves it to the orchestrator):** the drill's mode-2 check explains a post-restart write only if it is a schedule-triggered execution (no initiating user; trigger_key names a `job_schedule` row in the target and a slot inside the drill's D7-D9 window, per that schedule's cron and timezone) and the action results and audit events of that execution. Every other added or changed row stays unexplained. The job is never paused or rescheduled to avoid it (the ADR forbids that). The drill report lists every execution explained this way. The rule is disclosed in the handover. Repairs: ARCH (ADR-0064 amendment recording this decision), DO (drill and harness, tests that fail without the rule and that still flag an unexplained execution), AN (register notes and disclosure). Round 6 re-runs all three reviewers, qa included.
